# Article calculator call-out

When an article and a live calculator answer the same reader question, the last sentence of the copy must be followed by the shared call-out — before FAQ, newsletter, related reading, disclaimer, and footer.

## Do

- Add `calculatorCallout` to both `assets/i18n/en/articles/{slug}.json` and the FR file:
  `{ "href": "/calculators/{live-slug}/", "calculatorName": "Exact calculator title" }`
- Use one primary calculator. Secondary tools stay in related reading.
- Verify the href exists and does not overclaim what the tool models. If it omits a rule the article taught, add `note`.
- When shipping a new calculator that matches an existing article, add the call-out in the same change.
- When shipping a new article that has a matching live calculator, include `calculatorCallout` before publish.

## Do not

- Do not add a call-out when no live tool applies the article’s actual question.
- Do not invent a calculator, link a draft, or point at a generic nearby tool to fill the slot.
- Do not hand-build a second CTA card. The build injects `.article-calc-callout` from `calculatorCallout`.
- Do not place the call-out inside FAQ, related reading, or the footer.

## Copy

Default heading/lead live in `common.calculatorCallout`. Override `heading`, `lead` (`{name}`), or `note` only when the default would mislead.
